_BnF_Latin_9333_fol._83.jpg"}},"dish/ttongppang":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ttongppang","n":"Ttongppang","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from South Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ttongppang, or ddongbbang, is a novelty Korean street food. It is bread filled with red bean paste and walnut bits that is shaped like stylized human feces. It originated in Insa-dong, Seoul, South Korea."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ttongppang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ttongppang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Red bean paste","ingredient/red-bean-paste"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Korean Bapsang","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from South Korean cuisine","links":[["Chalbori-ppang","dish/chalbori-ppang"],["Chimaek","dish/chimaek"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dak-galbi","dish/dak-galbi"],["Gilgeori toast","dish/gilgeori-toast"],["Hodu-gwaja","dish/hodu-gwaja"],["Hwangnam-ppang","dish/hwangnam-ppang"],["Jinju bibimbap","dish/jinju-bibimbap"],["Jjolmyeon","dish/jjolmyeon"],["Kkulppang","dish/kkulppang"],["Milmyeon","dish/milmyeon"],["Rabokki","dish/rabokki"],["Ramyeon","dish/ramyeon"],["So-tteok-so-tteok","dish/so-tteok-so-tteok"],["Tornado potato","dish/tornado-potato"],["Yangnyeom chicken","dish/yangnyeom-chicken"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/4/44/Ttongppang%28Poo_Bun%2C_%EB%98%A5%EB%B9%B5%29_%287399937534%29.jpg/500px-Ttongppang%28Poo_Bun%2C_%EB%98%A5%EB%B9%B5%29_%287399937534%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Seongbin Im from Seoul, Korea, Republic of","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommon